From 1634de5abfe635a37d98a02cc6778c842d9b436f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 14:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: drop the postgres.h include from
 identifier_alpha_transfor.c
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c` (added by IvorySQL) includes
`postgres.h`, which transitively pulls in `utils/elog.h` →
`utils/errcodes.h`. The `errcodes.h` header is *generated* by a Meson
custom_target, and Meson does not propagate the dep ordering to
individual `.c.o` compile actions of `pgport`. Whether the file compiles
is a race against the `Generating ... errcodes` step.

Stock PG's port files include only `c.h` (which is enough for FRONTEND
built code: `Assert` + the `palloc → pg_malloc` macro from
`common/fe_memutils.h`). Match that pattern by dropping the unneeded
`postgres.h` include, which severs the stale-header dependency entirely.
---
 src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c b/src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c
index 9491b8c71f..6919294166 100644
--- a/src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c
+++ b/src/port/identifier_alpha_transfor.c
@@ -20,8 +20,6 @@
  */
 
 
-#include "postgres.h"
-
 #include "c.h"
 #include "common/fe_memutils.h"
 
